{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgJwrqXTrlNBozihKmyaY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Private list: nothing is outstanding. All ten screens exist and were inspected after the final edits, the copy matches the brief verbatim, the chips fit inside 375, and all 17 prototype reactions resolve to real frames with the splash set to both auto-advance and tap. There is no further tool call whose result another item would wait on, so this is the delivery report.\n\n**File:** https://www.figma.com/design/5I7PlvtoC7GX1zbReFo1tr/\n**Workspace page:** 03 · Workspace, ID `5:2`\n\nScreens, all 375 × 812, named exactly as the brief lists:\n\n| Screen | Node ID |\n|---|---|\n| 01_Splash | 19:198 |\n| 02_Welcome | 11:27 |\n| 03_Name | 11:47 |\n| 04_Home | 16:50 |\n| 05_Product_Quinoa | 16:163 |\n| 06_Basket | 16:204 |\n| 07_Checkout_Delivery | 19:213 |\n| 08_Checkout_Card | 19:277 |\n| 09_Order_Complete | 19:347 |\n| 10_Track_Order | 19:373 |\n\n**Design system.** I built 16 reusable components beside the screens: chips (selected and default), four icon buttons, favourite off/on, search field, filter button, row and combo product cards, basket row, stepper, and done/pending/current delivery steps. The given Button, Text Field, status bar and home indicator are used as instances; every call to action is an instance of the supplied Button, restyled for the outline variants. Brand is #FFA451 with Nunito throughout. Text uses #27214D with #5D577E for secondary copy, cream surfaces #FFF9F4 and #FFF1E4, hairlines #F0E9E2, and green #4CD964 for the success mark.\n\n**Prototype.** 17 click reactions plus a 2-second auto-advance on the splash:\n\n- Splash to Welcome, Welcome to Name, Name to Home\n- Home: Quinoa card to Product, basket icon to Basket\n- Product: back to Home, Add to basket to Basket\n- Basket: back to Home, Checkout to Delivery\n- Delivery: close to Basket, Pay with card to Card, Pay on delivery to Order complete\n- Card: close to Basket, Complete Order to Order complete\n- Order complete: Track order to Track order, Continue shopping to Home\n- Track order: back to Home\n\nFlow start is set to 01_Splash, named \"Fruit Hub\".\n\n**States covered:** Hottest chip selected, favourited vs unfavourited hearts, filled name field reading Tony, filled delivery and phone fields, all four filled card fields, both checkout sheets shown over a dimmed basket with the basket rows visible behind the scrim, and the delivery steps as done, done, current with the agent line and call button, then pending.\n\n**Limitations.** The brief marks menu, search, filter, non-Hottest categories, favourite toggles, Home add-to-basket, non-Quinoa combos and call agent as entry-only with no frames, so those have no destinations and I left them unwired. The two checkout sheets are separate frames that redraw the basket behind a scrim rather than Figma overlay connections. Reference pages 00, 01, 02 and 04 were left untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":4020,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":161746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4020}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"699ed9aa-c6dd-440c-b26c-c32602e1a158","uuid":"6379e183-4cf7-40f1-bdf5-76a7a6ac28d9","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:39:19.187Z"}
